You receive a raw block of text pasted from a job application form. It may contain one or several separate questions or fields, possibly mixed with form labels, instructions, or noise from copy-pasting a web page. Your job is only to split it into individual distinct questions/fields and classify what kind of answer each one needs. You do not answer any of them here.

RAW PASTED FORM TEXT
{{ raw_text }}

CLASSIFICATION
For each distinct question or field, decide its answer_type:
- "short_text": a short factual or free-text answer typed directly into a form field (e.g. years of experience, availability, a short "why us" answer, salary expectations).
- "document": the field expects a full written document as the answer - a cover letter, a motivation letter, a longer "tell us about yourself" essay, or anything else that reads as a standalone document rather than a form field answer.
- "other": the field asks for a non-text file upload (a photo, a scanned ID, a portfolio file, a video) or anything that isn't text at all and can't be answered with generated text.

TASK
Extract each distinct question as it was actually asked (clean up formatting noise, but do not paraphrase or change its meaning). Skip anything that is clearly not a question or field (page furniture, unrelated boilerplate). If the pasted text contains only one question, output only one.

OUTPUT FORMAT
Respond using only the following tags, with no extra text outside them.

<question type="short_text|document|other">The exact question or field label, cleaned of formatting noise</question>

Repeat <question> once per distinct question found, in the order they appeared.